---
title: Filspresso Next - Cross-Service Cryptographic Commitment Flow
---

sequenceDiagram
    participant NEST as NestJS Backend
    participant EGRESS as Egress Policy
    participant ASSERT as Service Assertions
    participant CONTRACT as Service Contracts
    participant RUST as Rust Crypto Service
    participant LEDGER as Security Ledger

    Note over NEST,RUST: CREATE COMMITMENT

    NEST->>EGRESS: assertAllowedEgress(http://rust-crypto:8090)
    Note over EGRESS: Check host against INTERNAL_EGRESS_ALLOWLIST<br/>Parse URL then extract hostname then match rule<br/>Wildcards: *.filspresso.local to filspresso.local
    EGRESS-->>NEST: Allowed

    NEST->>ASSERT: issueServiceAssertion(scope="service-crypto:commitment")
    Note over ASSERT: assertKeyUsage("service_assertion_signing",<br/>"issue_service_assertion", "service-crypto:commitment")<br/>Check KEY_USAGE_POLICY_JSON for allowed operations
    ASSERT-->>NEST: EdDSA JWT token<br/>{ iss, sub, aud, scope, iat, nbf, exp, jti, op_id }<br/>TTL: 120s default (30-600 configurable)

    NEST->>CONTRACT: assertServiceContract("rust_commitment_request_v1", payload)
    Note over CONTRACT: Schema validation for 8 contract types:<br/>go_ops_event_v1, kotlin_quote_v1,<br/>rust_commitment_request_v1, rust_verify_request_v1,<br/>invoice_render_v1, invoice_metadata_v1,<br/>repair_cost_change_v1, pii_anonymization_v1
    CONTRACT-->>NEST: Payload valid

    NEST->>RUST: POST /v1/commitment/sha3-256<br/>Headers: x-service-assertion, x-operation-id<br/>Body: { domain, payload }
    Note over NEST,RUST: Rust Crypto Service verifies

    activate RUST
        RUST->>RUST: decode_service_assertion(header)
        Note over RUST: Split JWT then verify EdDSA signature<br/>against SERVICE_ASSERTION_PUBLIC_KEY

        RUST->>RUST: check exp, nbf (time bounds)
        RUST->>RUST: verify aud equals "filspresso-backend"
        RUST->>RUST: verify iss in allowlist
        RUST->>RUST: verify scope equals "service-crypto:commitment"
        RUST->>RUST: verify jti not replayed (in-memory TTL cache)
        RUST->>RUST: verify op_id matches x-operation-id header

        RUST->>RUST: canonical_payload(payload)
        Note over RUST: Deterministic JSON serialization<br/>Recursively sort object keys

        RUST->>RUST: compute_commitment(domain, payload)
        Note over RUST: SHA3-256(domain + "|" + payload)
    deactivate RUST

    RUST-->>NEST: { commitment_hash, algorithm: "sha3-256" }

    NEST->>LEDGER: appendSecurityLedgerEvent(commitment)
    Note over LEDGER: SELECT prev_hash FOR UPDATE<br/>buildLedgerMaterial to SHA3-256<br/>INSERT with prev_hash, event_hash<br/>Immutable hash chain

    rect rgb(240, 245, 255)
        Note over NEST,RUST: VERIFY COMMITMENT<br/>Same flow but POST /v1/verify/sha3-256<br/>Returns { verified: bool, expected_hash, computed_hash }
    end

    rect rgb(255, 245, 240)
        Note over NEST,RUST: THRESHOLD OPERATION<br/>POST /v1/threshold/initiate to approve to execute<br/>Quorum-based M-of-N MPC with participant tracking<br/>ZK circuit registry: SHA3-256 hashed verification keys<br/>ZK proof verification with ledger anchoring<br/>MPC quorum with transcript signatures + rate limiting
    end

    rect rgb(245, 255, 245)
        Note over NEST,LEDGER: ARCHIVE FLOW<br/>Scheduled: runSecurityLedgerArchiveJob()<br/>SELECT events older than N hours<br/>Envelope-encrypt payload with VAULT_KEK<br/>Generate random DEK then AES-256-GCM encrypt payload<br/>Encrypt DEK with KEK<br/>INSERT into security_event_ledger_archive<br/>DELETE originals from security_event_ledger
    end
